import Mathlib

/-!
# A054096: T(n,2), array T as in A054090.

Source: https://oeis.org/A054096
Credit: @agchua

Comment line of A054096:
  Conjecture: sequence is A006183 shifted right. - Ralf Stephan, Jan 15 2004
Offset of A054096: 2 (data 1, 2, 6, 22, 98, 522, 3262, ...).

The array. A054090 (offset 0), name line: Triangular array generated by its row sums: T(n,0) = 1
for n >= 0, T(n,1) = r(n-1), T(n,k) = T(n,k-1) - (-1)^k * r(n-k) for k = 2, 3, ..., n, n >= 2,
r(h) = sum of the numbers in row h of T. Row h has the entries T(h,0), ..., T(h,h), so
r(h) = Sum_{j=0..h} T(h,j). The definition below is this, written with n+1 and k+2 for n and k;
the entries with k > n, which are not part of the triangle, are set to 0 and are never used
(the rows begin 1; 1, 1; 1, 2, 1; 1, 4, 2, 3; 1, 10, 6, 8, 7). A054096(n) = T(n,2), n >= 2.

The other sequence. A006183, offset 1, data 1, 2, 6, 22, 98, 522, ... Its name line reads
a(n) = (n+1)*a(n-1) + (2-n)*a(n-2); this recurrence produces the listed data when the terms are
numbered from 0 (a(0) = 1, a(1) = 2, as in its Mathematica program), so with the entry's offset 1
it reads a(n) = n*a(n-1) + (3-n)*a(n-2) for n >= 3, a(1) = 1, a(2) = 2, which is its Magma program
[n le 2 select n else n*Self(n-1)+(3-n)*Self(n-2): n in [1..30]]. The definition below is this
one, at the entry's offset 1 (the value at 0 is not used).

Shifted right: A054096(n) = A006183(n-1) for every n >= 2 (both lists start 1, 2, 6, 22, ...).
-/

namespace OMA.S_oeis_a054096

/-- The array A054090; r(h) is written out as Sum_{j=0..h} T(h,j). -/
def T : ℕ → ℕ → ℤ
  | _, 0 => 1
  | 0, _ + 1 => 0
  | n + 1, 1 => ∑ j ∈ Finset.range (n + 1), T n j
  | n + 1, k + 2 =>
    if k + 2 ≤ n + 1 then
      T (n + 1) (k + 1) -
        (-1) ^ (k + 2) * ∑ j ∈ Finset.range (n + 1 - (k + 2) + 1), T (n + 1 - (k + 2)) j
    else 0

/-- A054096(n) = T(n,2), n >= 2. -/
def a (n : ℕ) : ℤ := T n 2

/-- A006183 at its offset 1: a(1) = 1, a(2) = 2, a(n) = n*a(n-1) + (3-n)*a(n-2) for n >= 3. -/
def A006183 : ℕ → ℤ
  | 0 => 0
  | 1 => 1
  | 2 => 2
  | n + 3 => ((n : ℤ) + 3) * A006183 (n + 2) + (3 - ((n : ℤ) + 3)) * A006183 (n + 1)

/-- Stephan's conjecture: A054096 is A006183 shifted right. -/
theorem main : ∀ n : ℕ, 2 ≤ n → a n = A006183 (n - 1) := by
  sorry

end OMA.S_oeis_a054096
